# Launch consoles minimized (operator preference)

Operator preference (Phil, 2026-08-14): **minimize Windows Terminal hosts and
other console windows when you launch them so they do not interfere with other
windows.**

## The rule

> **When an agent or a script launches a new console window on Windows
> (conhost, Windows Terminal `wt.exe`, PowerShell/cmd windows, `Start-Process`
> of a console app, deploy/run helpers that open a server window), it MUST
> launch minimized (or hidden for true background) and MUST NOT steal focus
> from the operator's foreground window.**

This complements [`host-session-safety.mdc`](host-session-safety.mdc): do not
disrupt the interactive desktop session. Focus-stealing consoles that cover
Cursor, browsers, or other operator work are the same class of disruption as
killing tray apps or clearing session state.

## Practical guidance

| Need | Do this |
| --- | --- |
| Long-running server / agent / Vite / sink in its **own** OS window | `Start-Process … -WindowStyle Minimized` |
| Truly headless helper (no operator-visible console needed) | `Start-Process … -WindowStyle Hidden` (or `-NoNewWindow` when output stays in the caller) |
| Avoid | `-WindowStyle Normal` / `Maximized`; Activate / Raise / BringToFront after spawn |
| Out of scope | The agent's own Shell tool commands in the **integrated** terminal — this rule targets scripts/processes that spawn **new** OS console windows |

Preferred PowerShell shape:

```powershell
Start-Process -FilePath $exePath -WorkingDirectory $root -WindowStyle Minimized
```

For Windows Terminal hosts, pass the equivalent minimize / no-activate flags so
the new `wt.exe` tab or window does not come to the foreground.

## Forbidden constructs

- Launching server, agent, build, Vite, Mailpit, or similar console windows that
  pop to the **foreground** and cover the operator's other windows.
- Defaulting `Start-Process` (no `-WindowStyle`) for a new long-running console
  when Minimized would preserve function.
- Changing `-WindowStyle Hidden` on a genuine background helper to Normal so
  "you can see the logs" — leave Hidden; use Minimized only when a console must
  exist but should not steal focus.
- Treating UAC / elevation consent UI as something to hide — elevation prompts
  must remain visible when required. This rule does not waive that.

## Required agent behavior

1. When writing or editing a script that opens a **new** OS console for a
   long-running process, set `-WindowStyle Minimized` (or keep `Hidden` /
   `-NoNewWindow` when already headless).
2. Do not relaunch a healthy Running service solely to apply this style — the
   next launch picks it up.
3. Mirror this rule to `core-assets/.cursor/rules/` in the same change set
   ([`auto-commit-push.mdc`](auto-commit-push.mdc)) — the workspace `.cursor`
   directory is not a git root.

